  _ = `Steam Input`,
  _ = `To allow you to play any game, even if it doesn't support game controllers, your Deck uses <2>Steam Input</2>, a system that translates your physical inputs into commands for the game.`,
  _ = `Controller configuration for your <1></1> uses <2>Steam Input</2>, a system that translates your physical inputs into commands for the game. This allows you to play any game, even if it wasn't designed for your particular controller or doesn't support gamepads.`,
  _ = `<1>Commands</1> can be any kind of input that games use - a B button on a gamepad, the Enter key, a left mouse button click, and so on.`,
  _ = `Each game's Controller Layout contains a list of all the physical parts of your controller, and what commands are assigned to them.`,
  _ = `Customizing is as simple as selecting a physical input, and your desired command.`,
  _ = `Deck Verified games always have fully working Controller Layouts, so you can just fire them up and start playing.`,
  _ = `By default, they may not use the extra physical inputs the Deck has over standard gamepads, but the <1>Quick Settings</1> section makes it easy to assign commands for those.`,
  _ = `By default, they may not use the extra physical inputs the Deck has over standard gamepads, but the <1>Quick Settings</1> section makes it easy to assign commands for those.`,
  _ = `Commands`,
  _ = `Physical Inputs`,
  _ = `Enable Gyro`,
  _ = `Enable Back Grip Buttons`,
  _ = `Start Button`,
  _ = `Space`,
  _ = `Middle Mouse Click`,
  _ = `Controller Layout`,
  _ = `Non-Verified Games`,
  _ = `When playing non-verified games from your library, you may need to adjust your controller layout in order to make your game play better with your device’s controls.`,
  _ = `Our default templates work for most games, but otherwise we always suggest checking the game's Community Layouts to see if another player has published a custom layout.`,
  _ = `These games may ask you to press keys or buttons. In those cases, you’ll need to assign those commands to your device’s physical controls.`,
  _ = `Even when the game asks you to press a button that your device has, you will need to assign a matching command.`,
  _ = `Even when the game asks you to press a button that the <1></1> has, you will need to assign a matching command.`,
  _ = `Even when the game asks you to press a button that the Deck has, your layout may have a different command assigned to that physical button.`,
  _ = `Even when the game asks you to press a button that the <1></1> has, your layout may have a different command assigned to that physical button.`,
  _ = `F`,
  _ = `X Button`,
  _ = `It's often a good technique to find the in-game control settings, which will contain a list of all the commands the game expects.`,
  _ = `And then assign each of them to one of the Deck's physical inputs. `,
  _ = `But remember to always check the Community Layouts first - some other player has probably done this already.`,
  _ = `Press`,
  _ = `to Pay Respects`,
  _ = `Doubt`,
  _ = `Valve`,
  _ = `Official Layout for Team Fortress 2`,
  _ = `Standard Controls`,
  _ = `Gyro`,
  _ = `The gyro allows you to move the Deck itself to control a game. This can be very useful for fine control of a first or third person camera.`,
  _ = `The gyro allows you to move the gamepad itself to control a game. This can be very useful for fine control of a first or third person camera.`,
  _ = `By default, the gyro only sends input to the game when you're touching the <1>Right Joystick</1> or <2>Right Trackpad</2>. It's easy to change this behavior in the gyro settings, but we've found it to work well.`,
  _ = `By default, the gyro only sends input to the game when you're touching the <1>Right Trackpad</1>. It's easy to change this behavior in the gyro settings, but we've found it to work well.`,
  _ = `By default, the gyro always sends input to the game. It's easy to change this behavior in the gyro settings and depending on the game you might want to use a button to turn off the gyro in order to reposition controller without affecting your aim.`,
  _ = `You may want to plug in your controller`,
  _ = `The developer has indicated that this game only supports your <1>DualShock controller</1> over USB. If you wish to play the game with PlayStation glyphs, please plug the device in. If you continue via Bluetooth Steam will translate the controller into an Xbox device for the game`,
  _ = `The developer has indicated that this game only supports your <1>DualSense controller</1> over USB. If you wish to play the game with PlayStation glyphs, please plug the device in. If you continue via Bluetooth Steam will translate the controller into an Xbox device for the game.`,
  _ = `Controller using Steam Input`,
  _ = `Your <1>DualShock controller</1> isn’t supported by this game. Steam Input will translate the device so you will be able to play the game, but you may not see glyphs that match your device`,
  _ = `Your <1>DualSense controller</1> isn’t supported by this game. Steam Input will translate the device so you will be able to play the game, but you may not see glyphs that match your device`,
  _ = `This game has built-in support for your <1>DualShock controller</1>, but you have enabled Steam Input for PlayStation controllers. Steam Input will translate the device according to your configuration, but you may not see glyphs that match your device`,
  _ = `This game has built-in support for your <1>DualSense controller</1>, but you have enabled Steam Input for PlayStation controllers. Steam Input will translate the device according to your configuration, but you may not see glyphs that match your device`,
  _ = `The developer has indicated that this game supports your <1>DualShock controller</1> over USB, but you have enabled Steam Input for PlayStation controllers. If you wish to play the game with PlayStation glyphs, please plug the device in and disable Steam Input.`,
  _ = `The developer has indicated that this game supports your <1>DualSense controller</1> over USB. but you have enabled Steam Input for PlayStation controllers. If you wish to play the game with PlayStation glyphs, please plug the device in and disable Steam Input.`,
  _ = `Steam Remote Play`,
  _ = `Instead of running this game here, we'll stream it to you from a computer named '%1$s'.`,
  _ = `Your experience may vary depending on the network connection to the remote computer. You can find extra performance options in the Remote Play settings.`,
  _ = `On-Screen Keyboard`,
  _ = `To enter text in this game, you'll need to open the On-Screen Keyboard manually.`,
  _ = `Open the On-Screen Keyboard: `,
  _ = `Launchers`,
  _ = `This game's launcher does not support controller input. You can use the trackpad or touch screen to interact with it.`,
  _ = `This game's launcher does not support controller input. You can use the Guide Button chord to interact with it`,
  _ = `Open the On-Screen Keyboard: `,
