  _ = `Move Mouse by Amount`,
  _ = `Each time this command fires the mouse will move by a set number of pixels. This can be useful when you want to have a command to flip the direction your character is facing in an FPS game, or to click a specific item in a right-click menu in a management game.`,
  _ = `Move Mouse to Position`,
  _ = `When this command is fired the mouse will move to a specific location on screen. You can optionally have it remain in the new location, or return to where it was before the command fired. This essentially allows you to assign an on-screen, clickable button to your controller's physical input.`,
  _ = `X Position`,
  _ = `Y Position`,
  _ = `Return to previous position after command ends`,
  _ = `Manually select position`,
  _ = `Start`,
  _ = `Click mouse or hit %1$s to select the mouse position. %2$s or Escape to back out. Use %3$s / %4$s or the arrow keys to toggle between screenshots`,
  _ = `Reset Camera`,
  _ = `Reset Camera`,
  _ = `Reset the camera to the Horizon by maxing out the pitch of the camera, wait for a frame, and then return the camera to the horizon. This action requires the Dots Per 360° setting to be calibrated in either "Gyro to Mouse", or "FlickStick" modes. If the camera looks directly at the floor/ceiling, increase the Delay.`,
  _ = `Send -%1$s°, then wait %2$sms (equivalent to %3$sfps), then send %4$s°`,
  _ = `Delay`,
  _ = `Horizon Reset Angle`,
  _ = `Turn Camera %1$s°`,
  _ = `Turn Camera %1$s°`,
  _ = `This action will spin the camera by %1$s°, horizontally, by sending out %1$s° worth of Mouse Pixels over the duration of the turn. The "Dots Per 360°" setting determines how many pixels that is, so this action must be used in conjuction with Gyro to Mouse or FlickStick modes.`,
  _ = `Tip: to correctly tune the "Dots Per 360°" setting per game, set the "Spin Angle" to 360°.
 Press your "Turn Camera 360°" button in game. You should see a complete 360° turn.
 If you're not facing your initial direction after the spin, adjust the "Dots Per 360°" setting from the Controller Quick Settings Page and repeat the process until you get an accurate 360°.
 Now, "Gyro to Mouse", "Flick Stick", "Reset Camera" and "Face Direction" will all be accurate as well.`,
  _ = `Spin Angle`,
  _ = `Spin Duration`,
  _ = `Face Direction`,
  _ = `Turn Camera to Face Direction`,
  _ = `Turn the camera to face the direction of the input stick/trackpad/dpad/buttons direction. Adjust the Turn Duration to make the turn response shorter or longer. This action requires the Dots Per 360° setting to be calibrated in either Gyro to Mouse, or FlickStick modes.`,
