  _ = `Gyro Button Behavior - Toggle`,
  _ = `If set, the device's gyro will toggle its state each time the button is pressed.`,
  _ = `Mouse Sensitivity`,
  _ = `Sensitivity of the mouse cursor when the virtual joystick's output is set to Mouse.`,
  _ = `Sensitivity`,
  _ = `Sensitivity of the stick - how many camera degrees per second the camera will turn when fully deflected.`,
  _ = `Joystick Angles to Mouse Pixels (Dots Per 360°)`,
  _ = `At full deflection, the joystick will generate 360° of rotation over 1 second (when at 360° sensitivity). The Dots Per 360° value will convert the angles to mouse pixels. This value is shared with all other Dots Per 360° modes (in this Action Set). Tuning Tip: temporarily bind a button to the "Turn Camera 360°" action in the Mouse Actions tab to help calibrate the Gyro's real world angles with in-game angles.`,
  _ = `Enhance Small Movement Precision`,
  _ = `This will allow for finer grained control when making very small movements.  This must be tied with the Minimum Joystick X/Y Output Value to tune in to what a game expects for a small Joystick Value.  If Joystick X or Y Output Value is too high when combined with this setting, movement will be jittery even when not moving.  If it is too low, small movments will be missed entirely or very sluggish.  In combination with those settings, tune this value up to allow for very fine movements or down to reduce noise when trying to hold still.`,
  _ = `Custom Response Curve`,
  _ = `Games will sometimes have varying response curves for their joystick input.  For best Mouse-Like Joystick response, linear response is the most 1:1.  This setting can be altered to try to compensate for a game's built in response curve.  Generally this setting should be used as a last resort, but can be slid to the right to compensate for what feels like unwanted acceleration or poor initial response or slid to the left to compensate for inverted acceleration.`,
  _ = `Full Pull`,
  _ = `Soft Pull`,
  _ = `Single Button`,
  _ = `This input will act as a single button with commands for both touch and click events.`,
  _ = `Click`,
  _ = `This command will be sent when the pad is clicked.`,
  _ = `Touch`,
  _ = `This command will be sent when the pad is touched.`,
  _ = `Style of Input - Joystick Camera`,
  _ = `This input will operate as a joystick optimized for controlling a first or third person camera.  Joystick will only work with XInput compatible gamepad games.`,
