  _ = `Trigger Dampening Off`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is Disabled`,
  _ = `Trigger Soft Pull Dampening Right`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is enabled for the Right Trigger Soft Pull.  Squeezing the trigger will dampen any mouse movements until a full click is engaged.`,
  _ = `Trigger Soft Pull Dampening Left`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is enabled for the Left Trigger Soft Pull.  Squeezing the trigger will dampen any mouse movements until a full click is engaged.`,
  _ = `Trigger Soft Pull Dampening Both`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is enabled for the Both Triggers Soft Pull.  Squeezing either trigger will dampen any mouse movements until a full click is engaged.`,
  _ = `Trigger Soft/Full Pull Dampening Right`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is enabled for the Right Trigger Soft/Full Pull.  Squeezing the trigger including clicking will dampen any mouse movements until fully released.`,
  _ = `Trigger Soft/Full Pull Dampening Left`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is enabled for the Left Trigger Soft/Full Pull.  Squeezing the trigger including clicking will dampen any mouse movements until fully released.`,
  _ = `Trigger Soft/Full Pull Dampening Both`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is enabled for the Both Triggers Soft/Full Pull.  Squeezing either trigger including clicking will dampen any mouse movements until fully released.`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening Amount`,
  _ = `This sets how much the mouse movement should be dampened.  Slide to the right to further stop mouse movement.`,
  _ = `Touch`,
  _ = `A command can be sent while touching the pad.  If momentum/trackball mode is active, these buttons will be released when it fully decays.  Otherwise, these buttons will be released the moment you stop touching the pad.`,
  _ = `Gyro Lean Point`,
  _ = `This determines how far the controller must be turned to trigger lean commands.`,
  _ = `Lean Right`,
  _ = `You can trigger this command when tilting the controller in the axis you aren't using for control.`,
  _ = `Lean Left`,
  _ = `You can trigger this command when tilting the controller in the axis you aren't using for control.`,
  _ = `Trackball Mode`,
  _ = `Trackball mode makes the pad act like a trackball instead of a mouse.  It will have momentum and friction, allowing you to flick it like a trackball.`,
  _ = `Trackball Mode - On`,
  _ = `The mouse will move like a trackball.  It will have momentum and friction and can be flicked like a trackball.`,
  _ = `Trackball Mode - Off`,
  _ = `The mouse will move like a normal mouse.  It will have not have momentum or friction.`,
  _ = `Sensitivity`,
  _ = `Sets the sensitivity of this control.  NOTE: Since this mode is sending the game joystick output - the maximum sensitivity will be limited by the game's Gamepad Camera Sensitivity.  For best results, set the in-game Gamepad Camera Sensitivity option as high as possible.`,
  _ = `Rotation`,
  _ = `Rotation is the horizon line of mouse movement.  Swiping your thumb over the trackpad may result in a slighly canted movement.  You can align this rotation to match your natural movements, so that a quick swipe results in a perfectly horizontal mouse movement.`,
  _ = `Haptic Intensity`,
  _ = `This sets the intensity of the haptics.`,
  _ = `Haptic Intensity - Off`,
  _ = `Do not use haptics for this mode.`,
  _ = `Haptic Intensity - Low`,
  _ = `Use low intensity haptics.`,
  _ = `Haptic Intensity - Medium`,
  _ = `Use medium intensity haptics.`,
  _ = `Haptic Intensity - High`,
  _ = `Use High intensity haptics.`,
  _ = `Click`,
  _ = `This command will be performed when you click the pad/stick.`,
  _ = `Lean Left Command`,
  _ = `This command will be performed when you lean the controller to the left.`,
  _ = `Lean Right Command`,
  _ = `This command will be performed when you lean the controller to the right.`,
  _ = `Trackball Friction`,
  _ = `Trackball friction determines how quickly the trackball slows to a stop when freely spinning.`,
  _ = `Trackball Friction - Off`,
  _ = `If off the trackball will have no momentum.  It will act as if trackball mode is disabled.`,
  _ = `Trackball Friction - Low`,
  _ = `With Low Friction, the trackball will continue to rotate for a long period after being flicked, slowly coming to a stop.`,
  _ = `Trackball Friction - Medium`,
  _ = `With Medium Friction, the trackball will rotate for a period after being flicked, gradually coming to a stop.`,
  _ = `Trackball Friction - High`,
  _ = `With High Friction, the trackball will spin for a short duration, quickly come to a stop after being flicked.`,
  _ = `Trackball Friction - None`,
  _ = `With No Friction, the trackball will spin forever after being flicked without outside intervention.`,
  _ = `Vertical Friction Scale`,
  _ = `Vertical Friction determines how fast the vertical movement comes to a stop relative to horizontal movement.  At 50% along the slider it is equal, if less than half it will slow less quickly, if more, more quickly.  For games were you control the camera, it is usually desirable to have high vertical friction so flicks are primarily used for spinning the camera along the horizontal axis.`,
  _ = `Vertical Sensitivity Scale`,
  _ = `Vertical Sensitivity Scale determines how much vertical movement occurs relative to horizontal movement.  At 50% along the slider it is equal, if less than half it vertical movement will be lower than horizontal, while more will increase the ratio to more vertical movement.`,
  _ = `Smoothing`,
  _ = `Smoothing helps to remove noise and jitter from the mouse.  Smaller values will result in less filtering, while higher values will be more filtered and smoother.`,
  _ = `Acceleration`,
  _ = `Acceleration will cause faster movements to cause more mouse movement relative to slow movements for the same space covered on the pad.`,
  _ = `Acceleration - Off`,
  _ = `With no acceleration movement will be 1:1, with the distance covered on the pad always resulting in the same in-game output regardless of the speed.`,
  _ = `Acceleration - Low`,
  _ = `With low acceleration movement will be slightly accelerated, with faster movements making in-game output slightly greater at faster speeds for the same distance covered on the physical pad.`,
  _ = `Acceleration - Medium`,
  _ = `With medium acceleration movement will be fairly accelerated, with faster movements making in-game output quite a bit greater at faster speeds for the same distance covered on the physical pad.`,
  _ = `Acceleration - High`,
  _ = `With high acceleration movement will be very accelerated, with faster movements making in-game output extremely high at faster speeds for the same distance covered on the physical pad.`,
