  _ = `Trigger Dampening On`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is Enabled`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening Off`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is Disabled`,
  _ = `Trigger Soft Pull Dampening Right`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is enabled for the Right Trigger Soft Pull.  Squeezing the trigger will dampen any mouse movements until a full click is engaged.`,
  _ = `Trigger Soft Pull Dampening Left`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is enabled for the Left Trigger Soft Pull.  Squeezing the trigger will dampen any mouse movements until a full click is engaged.`,
  _ = `Trigger Soft Pull Dampening Both`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is enabled for the Both Triggers Soft Pull.  Squeezing either trigger will dampen any mouse movements until a full click is engaged.`,
  _ = `Trigger Soft/Full Pull Dampening Right`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is enabled for the Right Trigger Soft/Full Pull.  Squeezing the trigger including clicking will dampen any mouse movements until fully released.`,
  _ = `Trigger Soft/Full Pull Dampening Left`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is enabled for the Left Trigger Soft/Full Pull.  Squeezing the trigger including clicking will dampen any mouse movements until fully released.`,
  _ = `Trigger Soft/Full Pull Dampening Both`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening is enabled for the Both Triggers Soft/Full Pull.  Squeezing either trigger including clicking will dampen any mouse movements until fully released.`,
  _ = `Trigger Dampening Amount`,
  _ = `This sets how much the mouse movement should be dampened.  Slide to the right to further stop mouse movement.`,
  _ = `Minimum Joystick X Output Value`,
  _ = `This value determines the minimum amount the output joystick will send when swiping.  The ideal setting is adjusting it so the game's built in deadzone is exactly compensated for.  Adjust this value upwards until slow movements don't stop or stutter, but provide clean movement.  Move down if small movements are too big.  Also see the Enhance Small Movements setting.`,
  _ = `Minimum Joystick Y Output Value`,
  _ = `This value determines the minimum amount the output joystick will send when swiping.  The ideal setting is adjusting it so the game's built in deadzone is exactly compensated for.  Adjust this value upwards until slow movements don't stop or stutter, but provide clean movement.  Move down if small movements are too big.  Also see the Enhance Small Movements setting.`,
  _ = `Style of Input - Mouse Joystick`,
  _ = `This input feels like a mouse, but outputs a joystick.  This is intended for games which do not allow simultaneous mouse and gamepad inputs.  It's the next best option to the real thing for providing an emulated 1:1 response.  NOTE: Since this mode is seen by the game as a joystick, the sensitivity response is limited by the game's gamepad sensitivity settings.  For best results, set the in-game gamepad camera sensitivity to the highest value possible.`,
  _ = `Style of Input - Mouse`,
  _ = `This input translates a joystick into mouse or cursor output. NOTE: This input may be affected by both the layout's sensitivity and the in-game mouse sensitivity`,
  _ = `Gyro Output Scale`,
  _ = `When using in combination with a pad also using Mouse Joystick mode, use this setting to scale the relative input of the gyro to be less or greater.`,
  _ = `Gyro Sensitivity`,
  _ = ``,
  _ = `Use Controller Preferences`,
  _ = `All gyro modes have common settings for sensitivity, smoothing, acceleration, and angle offset.  If this is set, the settings from the controller preferences will be used instead of the mode specific settings.`,
  _ = `Gyro ° Sensitivity`,
  _ = `When "Dots Per 360°" is correctly calibrated in game, this will multiply the output of the gyro to the mouse. 1x will give 1:1 real world gyro rotation to in world rotation. 2x will turn the in world camera twice as fast as the controller's rotation.`,
  _ = `Gyro ° Sensitivity`,
  _ = `When "In-Game Max Turn Rate" is correctly calibrated in game, this will multiply the output of the gyro to the mouse. 1x will give 1:1 real world gyro rotation to in game rotation. 2x will turn the in world camera twice as fast as the controller's rotation.`,
  _ = `Gyro Lean Point`,
  _ = `This determines how far the controller must be turned to trigger lean commands.`,
  _ = `Button Behavior`,
  _ = `The gyro input button behavior can be flipped.  If set to off, gyro will turn off when the button is pressed.`,
  _ = `Gyro Button Behavior - On`,
  _ = `If set, the device's gyro will turn on when the button is pressed.`,
  _ = `Gyro Button Behavior - Off`,
  _ = `If set, the device's gyro will turn off when the button is pressed.`,
  _ = `Gyro Button Behavior - Toggle`,
  _ = `If set, the device's gyro will toggle between being enabled or disabled when the button is pressed.`,
  _ = `Horizontal Scale`,
  _ = `Scale the horizontal sensitivity.  This will change the motion of the horizontal axis relative to the vertical.`,
  _ = `Vertical Scale`,
  _ = `Scale the vertical sensitivity. This will change the motion of the vertical axis relative to the horizontal.`,
  _ = `Lean Right`,
  _ = `You can trigger this command when tilting the controller in the axis you aren't using for control.`,
  _ = `Lean Left`,
  _ = `You can trigger this command when tilting the controller in the axis you aren't using for control.`,
