  _ = `Touch`,
  _ = `Style of Input - Mouse Region`,
  _ = `This input will act as a Mouse Region.  Mouse Region sends mouse input to a game, but treats the pad as a 1:1 map to screen space, so touching a particular place on the pad will always put the cursor in the same place on the screen.  In addition to working great for top-down style games, regions can be restricted to certain areas of the screen, scaled, stretched and mode-shifted in to select mini-maps, toolbars, inventory, etc.`,
  _ = `Click`,
  _ = `This command will be performed when you click the pad/stick.`,
  _ = `Region Size`,
  _ = `This will scale the size of the region that is mapped to the outer extents of the pad/stick.`,
  _ = `Region Horizontal Position`,
  _ = `This is the on screen horizontal position that the region will be centered around.`,
  _ = `Region Vertical Position`,
  _ = `This is the on screen vertical position that the region will be centered around.`,
  _ = `Snap Cursor on Activation`,
  _ = `Snap Cursor on Activation`,
  _ = `Snap Cursor on Activation`,
  _ = `When activated, should the mouse cursor be snapped to the center of the region?`,
  _ = `Snap mouse cursor to the center of the region on mode activation`,
  _ = `Remain in current mouse position`,
  _ = `Return Cursor on Deactivation`,
  _ = `When you stop touching or disable the mode shift, should the mouse be snapped back to the position it was before the mode shift was engaged?`,
  _ = `Snap Back Enabled`,
  _ = `This will snap back the mouse to the previous position on the release of the trackpad or end of the mode shift.`,
  _ = `Snap Back Disabled`,
  _ = `This will leave the mouse postition as-is on the release of the trackpad or end of the mode shift.`,
  _ = `Horizontal Scale`,
  _ = `Scale the horizontal region.  You can use this to change the on-screen region from a circle to an ellipse or a line.`,
  _ = `Rotate Output`,
  _ = `Rotates the output to the joystick, such that pushing the physical stick "North" results in an output of "East", when set to 90°`,
  _ = `Vertical Scale`,
  _ = `Scale the vertical region.  You can use this to change the on-screen region from a circle to an ellipse or a line.`,
  _ = `Invert Horizontal`,
  _ = `Flip inputs to the region horizontally.`,
  _ = `Invert Vertical`,
  _ = `Flip inputs to the region vertically.`,
  _ = `Touch`,
  _ = `A command sent while touching the pad.  Commands are 'held down' until you stop touching, which is useful for moving your player.`,
  _ = `Style of Input - Radial Menu`,
  _ = `This input will act as a Radial Menu.  Radial Menus display on-screen when your finger touches the Touch Pad.  Clicking on one of the shown buttons will fire off the appropriate command.  RadialMenus can have a variety of buttons, layouts, size, opacity, and can use icons.`,
