  _ = `Activator Type`,
  _ = `Activators determine how the input responds to you.  Is it a regular press, a long press, a double tap?  Select them here or remove them.`,
  _ = `None - Remove Activator`,
  _ = `Selecting this option will remove the activator and any commands it contains.`,
  _ = `Regular Press`,
  _ = `Regular Press Activator are the default type.  When you press the button, it activates and stays on until you release it.`,
  _ = `Double Press`,
  _ = `Double Press Activator requires a quick double tap of the input to activate.  If held on the second press, it will remain pressed.  Any interruptable activators on the same button will not fire if a double press is fired, and will be paused until the double press time has passed.`,
  _ = `Long Press`,
  _ = `Long Press Activator requires the button to be held for a period of time to activate.  Once the long press time has passed, it will activate stay on until you release it.  Any interruptable activators on the same button will not fire if a long press is fired, and will be paused until the button is released while under the long press time.`,
  _ = `Start Press`,
  _ = `Start Press Activator activates when the button is pressed.  It is immediately deactivates even if the button continues to be held.  This is useful, particularly when used with a Release Press Activator, to convert a Toggle into a Hold, such as a Toggle Crouch command.`,
  _ = `Release Press`,
  _ = `Release Press Activator activates and deactivates when the button is released.`,
  _ = `Soft Press`,
  _ = `Soft Press Activator activates when the button or trigger is pressed partway.`,
  _ = `Analog`,
  _ = `Analog Activator produces an analog output.`,
  _ = `Button Chord`,
  _ = `Button Chord Activator activates when the both the button owning the activator and the chorded button are pressed.`,
  _ = `Command`,
  _ = `You can assign one or more commands to this activator.`,
  _ = `Activate Analog Stick/Trackpad`,
  _ = `Virtual controllers can create a virtual thumbstick or trackpad under a button while it is pressed. This is good for machineguns that can be aimed with the same finger that's holding down the trigger.`,
  _ = `No Analog Stick/Trackpad`,
  _ = `This activator behaves normally and doesn't activate a virtual analog stick or trackpad.`,
  _ = `Activate Left Analog Stick`,
  _ = `While these buttons are held the same finger will also control the virtual left analog stick.`,
  _ = `Activate Right Analog Stick`,
  _ = `While these buttons are held the same finger will also control the virtual right analog stick.`,
  _ = `Activate Center Trackpad`,
  _ = `While these buttons are held the same finger will also control the center virtual trackpad.`,
  _ = `Activate Left Trackpad`,
  _ = `While these buttons are held the same finger will also control the left virtual trackpad.`,
  _ = `Activate Right Trackpad`,
  _ = `While these buttons are held the same finger will also control the right virtual trackpad.`,
  _ = `Toggle`,
  _ = `Toggle will make this activator continue to be active after releasing it until it is pressed again.`,
  _ = `Toggle - On`,
  _ = `This activator continues to be active after releasing it until it is pressed again.`,
  _ = `Toggle - Off`,
  _ = `This activator will act as a tradition button where it is held on until the button is released.`,
  _ = `Invert Input`,
  _ = `Invert the input: Releasing the button will activate the command while pressing it will deactivate the command.`,
  _ = `Interruptable`,
  _ = `Interruptable activators can be paused or stopped by other activators.  For example, a Long Press activator can interrupt a Full Press activator so the Full Press only fires if the Long Press doesn't.  If not interruptable, it ignores the other activator in regards to behavior.`,
  _ = `Interruptable - On`,
  _ = `This activator will pause or not fire at all if other activators are in play.  Long Press, Double Press, etc. will cause it to wait for their conditions to be met before this activator is allowed to activate itself.  If those other activators fire, this one will not.`,
  _ = `Interruptable - Off`,
  _ = `This activator will ignore other activators and always activate/deactivate as if it were alone.`,
  _ = `Fire Start Delay`,
  _ = `The activator will wait for this period of time after the button has been pressed before activating.  This delay will offset the entire period the button is held, so if no end delay is set, the total period of time the button is held will be the same, just delayed.`,
  _ = `Fire End Delay`,
  _ = `The activator will wait for this period of time after the button has been released before deactivating.  The end delay will make a button be active for longer than it was physically held.`,
  _ = `Haptics Intensity`,
  _ = `This defines the strength of haptics on activation and deactivation of the activator.`,
  _ = `Haptics Intensity - Off`,
  _ = `No haptics.`,
  _ = `Haptics Intensity - Low`,
  _ = `Low haptics on activation and deactivation of the activator.`,
  _ = `Haptics Intensity - Medium`,
  _ = `Medium haptics on activation and deactivation of the activator.`,
  _ = `Haptics Intensity - High`,
  _ = `High haptics on activation and deactivation of the activator.`,
  _ = `Activate Analog Stick/Trackpad`,
  _ = `Cycle Commands`,
  _ = `Cycle Commands will make this activator cycle through each of its commands each time it is activated, in the order listed in the Layout.`,
